WITS screens for unequal access to information, biased ground rules, and impaired objectivity during new-business review and whenever circumstances change. For this work we would add a check before each package assignment. The Task Lead would compare the provider, its parent, its assessor, and key dependencies against:
(1) a register of contracts, subcontracts, teaming, advisory, implementation, and resale relationships for WITS, affiliates, and subcontractors;
(2) signed attestations from assigned staff covering prior employers, financial interests, outside work, and earlier package involvement;
(3) subcontractor certifications.
The register covers relationships such as our DOE order for licensed OPEXUS FOIAXpress SaaS, so a package from that provider would trigger review. Any match goes to WITS corporate management and, when Government work is affected, in writing to the Contracting Officer before work starts. Mitigation may include recusal, reassignment, access restrictions, firewalls, or declining the review, and we would rely on it only after the Government accepts it. We would log each clearance and repeat it when ownership or assignments change.
